\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Performance on the fixed internal holdout (175 patients, 56 pCR positive). For each patient and landmark, the five seed44 fold-model probabilities are averaged before computing any metric. Macro averages T0--T2 metrics. AP denotes average precision; F1 uses threshold 0.5. Entries are point estimates; paired differences, patient intervals, and multiplicity-adjusted significance are reported in Table~\ref {tab:bootstrap}.}}{11}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{2}{11}{Performance on the fixed internal holdout (175 patients, 56 pCR positive). For each patient and landmark, the five seed44 fold-model probabilities are averaged before computing any metric. Macro averages T0--T2 metrics. AP denotes average precision; F1 uses threshold 0.5. Entries are point estimates; paired differences, patient intervals, and multiplicity-adjusted significance are reported in Table~\ref {tab:bootstrap}}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Discrimination of seed-44 five-fold probability ensembles. (A--C) ROC curves; (D--F) precision--recall curves. Each patient's probabilities are averaged across the five fold models before constructing a curve or computing a metric. Shading shows pointwise 95\% paired patient-bootstrap intervals conditional on the fitted ensemble. Colored values give AUROC or non-interpolated AP calculated directly from ensemble scores; grid interpolation may change the plotted area. The dotted PR reference is the 0.32 positive prevalence.}}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:discrimination}{{2}{11}{Discrimination of seed-44 five-fold probability ensembles. (A--C) ROC curves; (D--F) precision--recall curves. Each patient's probabilities are averaged across the five fold models before constructing a curve or computing a metric. Shading shows pointwise 95\% paired patient-bootstrap intervals conditional on the fitted ensemble. Colored values give AUROC or non-interpolated AP calculated directly from ensemble scores; grid interpolation may change the plotted area. The dotted PR reference is the 0.32 positive prevalence}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Exploratory principal Macro comparisons. AUROC uses paired DeLong tests with correlated landmark placements averaged per patient. AP and F1 use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests with 99,999 shared resamples. All $p$ values are two-sided. Holm adjustment covers all nine entries in this table. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm  {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fitted, retrospectively selected seed44 ensembles.}}{12}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bootstrap}{{3}{12}{Exploratory principal Macro comparisons. AUROC uses paired DeLong tests with correlated landmark placements averaged per patient. AP and F1 use approximate, null-centered paired patient-bootstrap tests with 99,999 shared resamples. All $p$ values are two-sided. Holm adjustment covers all nine entries in this table. Direct and Attention abbreviate DirectReadout and ForecastAttention. $^{*}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.05$, $^{**}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.01$, $^{***}p_{\mathrm {Holm}}<0.001$; ns, not significant after the stated correction. Intervals are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals (2,000 shared draws) and need not agree with adjusted test decisions. All analyses condition on the fitted, retrospectively selected seed44 ensembles}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Paired differences between seed-44 ensembles at T0, T1, T2, and the landmark macro. Colors distinguish auxiliary supervision, additional forecast readout, and the complete-model contrast. Squares denote macro estimates. Bars are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals with identical patient draws shared across models and landmarks; adjusted tests are reported separately in Tables~\ref {tab:bootstrap} and~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}. Five constituent fold models do not represent five independent test cohorts.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paired}{{3}{12}{Paired differences between seed-44 ensembles at T0, T1, T2, and the landmark macro. Colors distinguish auxiliary supervision, additional forecast readout, and the complete-model contrast. Squares denote macro estimates. Bars are unadjusted 95\% patient-bootstrap intervals with identical patient draws shared across models and landmarks; adjusted tests are reported separately in Tables~\ref {tab:bootstrap} and~\ref {tab:significance_landmarks}. Five constituent fold models do not represent five independent test cohorts}{figure.3}{}}
