\newlabel{fig:subgroups}{{5}{15}{Exploratory subgroup and operating-point summaries from seed-44 ensemble probabilities. (A) Macro AUROC differences between ForecastAttention and NoJEPA within HR/HER2 and age groups, with sample sizes, positive outcomes, and unadjusted paired intervals. No subgroup-interaction claim is made. (B) Specificity and sensitivity at threshold 0.5 across landmarks; colors identify models and markers identify landmarks}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Archived seed-44 fixed-training-probe diagnostics. (A) Copy-normalized forecast skill at common epoch 20. (B) Predictor gradient norms from pCR and weighted rollout losses. (C) Three-step skill across common archived epochs. Statistics are computed within each model's EMA coordinates and averaged across five folds, distinct from probability ensembling for pCR. These are training diagnostics; real continuous visit chains are required and three-step eligibility is only 5--9 patients per probe.}}{15}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{6}{15}{Archived seed-44 fixed-training-probe diagnostics. (A) Copy-normalized forecast skill at common epoch 20. (B) Predictor gradient norms from pCR and weighted rollout losses. (C) Three-step skill across common archived epochs. Statistics are computed within each model's EMA coordinates and averaged across five folds, distinct from probability ensembling for pCR. These are training diagnostics; real continuous visit chains are required and three-step eligibility is only 5--9 patients per probe}{figure.6}{}}
